==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_NoSelfApproval  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoSelfApproval.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoSelfApproval allows Alloy to construct a world where a PatchStatus operation succeeds even though the caller is the same user as the application's applicant — the self-approval conflict-of-interest violation that FCA framing requires cannot happen.
    expected to FAIL: NoSelfMutation, FR_013_NoSelfApproval
      - NoSelfMutation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_013_NoSelfApproval: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries lets Alloy invent two distinct AuditEntries for the same application that share an identical (prevStatus, newStatus) pair — the hallmark of an in-place update or duplicated replay that the append-only invariant is designed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditCompleteness allows a LoanApplication to exist with no AuditEntry at all — violating the invariant that every observable state change must have a corresponding audit record (SC-002, SC-008).
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_016_InitialAuditEntry
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_016_InitialAuditEntry: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing F_PermissionMatrix lets Alloy assign arbitrary allow-cells to the PermMatrix, including granting Auditor access to PatchStatus or Applicant access to GetAudit, breaking every LeastPrivilege and role-isolation assertion.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PermissionCompleteness, PermissionGrounding, FR_005_AuditorReadOnly, FR_023_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionGrounding: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AuditorReadOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_023_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_RoleMutualExclusivity  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_RoleMutualExclusivity.als
    rationale: Removing F_RoleMutualExclusivity allows Alloy to construct a User who simultaneously holds both Officer and Auditor roles, violating the data-model constraint that these two bank-staff roles are mutually exclusive.
    expected to FAIL: FR_002_RoleMutualExclusivity
      - FR_002_RoleMutualExclusivity: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoInformationLeakage  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoInformationLeakage.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoInformationLeakage allows a non-owner applicant's GET to succeed on an application they don't own, meaning the system distinguishes 'exists but not yours' from 'does not exist' — precisely the privacy invariant FR-020/FR-021 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)

